  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.2: Additive observability and a typed failure taxonomy — crypto core unchanged (ML-DSA-65 signatures, X-Wing + AES-256-GCM optional encryption, sign-then-encrypt, RFC 7516 AAD binding, fail-closed validation), no new algorithm suite, no algorithm agility. New: validation metrics via System.Diagnostics.Metrics (meter \"PostQuantum.Jwt\", counter \"pqjwt.validations\" tagged outcome=success|failure and a coarse, bounded, non-sensitive reason) — opt in with any OpenTelemetry/meter listener, no new dependency. New public PqJwtFailureReason enum + PqJwtValidationException.Reason so callers (and the metric) categorize failures from a typed value rather than parsing messages; the fail-closed control flow is byte-for-byte unchanged. Also adds a runnable samples/ suite, a `dotnet new` template package (PostQuantum.Jwt.Templates: pqjwt-webapi, pqjwt-console), and expanded SECURE-USAGE / HARDENING-CHECKLIST guidance. The preview.N suffix continues to carry the maturity caveat: NOT independently audited, NOT for production. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
